//
// PROBE: the rest of the `.` folds -- `**.`, `*-.`, `*/.` and `Σ.` -- and
// `?false*.`, the workbench form of the non-negating `notifthenelse` (F97).
//
// A `.` fold pulls its accumulator from the workbench and every operand from
// the stack, and puts the accumulator back on the workbench when the stack
// runs out (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/math/math_op.rs:22-76).
// `take` brings it back to print. `Σ.` aliases `*+.`
// (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/create_aliases.rs:39), and
// `?false*.` aliases `notifthenelse.`
// (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/create_aliases.rs:17). Its
// condition is on the workbench, and true runs the lambda on top.
//
"probe: **. multiplies into the workbench accumulator" println
2 3 4 . **. take println
"probe: *-. subtracts, operands in the order - takes them" println
10 3 1 . *-. take println
"probe: */. divides" println
100 2 5.0 . */. take println
"probe: Σ. is *+." println
1 2 3 . Σ. take println
"probe: ?false*. takes its condition from the workbench and does not negate" println
true . { "A" } { "B" } ?false*. println
false . { "A" } { "B" } ?false*. println
